---
references:
  book:
    id: book
    type: book
    title: A Book
  paper:
    id: paper
    type: article
    title: A Paper
---

Frontmatter references are authored for *this* document, so the `references`
export carries all of them by default (`references_scope = "all"`, §2.6 of
RFC-0002). `paper` is never cited below, yet it still ships:

Minim [^book "hlm. 45"] esse do ut anim proident.

`references_scope = "cited"` would drop `paper` from that export. The setting
never touches `citations`, `reference_id` or `citation_number`.
